HOTD4 Special Rev B (DVP-0010B, game ID 0x7d6ab3e3): the fixes of 0005 and 0006 for the same engine. The Special has the
same multitexture loop as HOTD4 Rev C (0x082e79a9..0x082e7ac9, same instructions; the path ends with the call at 0x082e7acf to
the depth-state reset 0x08326ed8), the same single glXGetProcAddressARB call (0x081fc0f5) and the same standard shader
(fs/dat/std.dat0 with "Standard Vertex Shader", the same varyings and the same main() header). Both fixes are applied only
when the bytes at those call sites are the expected calls. Applies after 0006.
Measured 2026-10-21 (headless, daemon): without this patch the ride safety and story screens draw as grey and white boxes,
the first stage has purple-blue/green surfaces and a whitish picture; with it those screens, the HUD and the stage render
correctly (start log native-HOTD4SP-20261021-144448.log).

--- a/src/lindbergh/patch.c
+++ b/src/lindbergh/patch.c
@@ -42,6 +42,8 @@
 // The call at 0x082a0b90 (to the depth-state reset 0x082dca9a) is the last step of that path; this replacement first disables
 // GL_TEXTURE_2D on texture units 1..N again (active unit kept), then does the original call. Measured on the bench, 2026-10-20.
 void *hod4GetProcAddressARB(const unsigned char *procName); // shaderPatches.c (RavenGun)
+// HOTD4 Special Rev B has the same path (loop 0x082e79a9..0x082e7ac9, the reset at 0x08326ed8); its case below points
+// hod4DepthStateReset there before it patches the call (RavenGun 0007).
 static void (*hod4DepthStateReset)(void) = (void (*)(void))0x082dca9a;
 __attribute__((force_align_arg_pointer)) static void hod4MultitexDone(void)
 {
@@ -2846,6 +2848,20 @@
 
             // Shader Fixes
             cacheModedShaderFiles();
+
+            // RavenGun 0007: the same leaked texture units as HOTD4 Rev C (hod4MultitexDone). The multitexture path ends with
+            // the call at 0x082e7acf to the depth-state reset 0x08326ed8 (e8 04 f4 03 00); only when those bytes are there.
+            if (memcmp((void *)0x082e7acf, "\xe8\x04\xf4\x03\x00", 5) == 0)
+            {
+                hod4DepthStateReset = (void (*)(void))0x08326ed8;
+                replaceCallAtAddress(0x082e7acf, hod4MultitexDone);
+            }
+
+            // RavenGun 0007: the game's one glXGetProcAddressARB call (0x081fc0f5, e8 16 0e e5 ff = call 0x0804cf10) through
+            // hod4GetProcAddressARB, so glShaderSourceARB gets the standard-shader fix (shaderPatches.c), as in HOTD4 Rev C.
+            if (memcmp((void *)0x081fc0f5, "\xe8\x16\x0e\xe5\xff", 5) == 0)
+                replaceCallAtAddress(0x081fc0f5, hod4GetProcAddressARB);
+
             if (getConfig()->cpuFreqGhz != 0.0f)
             {
                 uint32_t cpuFreq = (uint32_t)(getConfig()->cpuFreqGhz * 998000000.0);
